// A `.map` whose callback returns a list builds a list of lists: a ref list whose element is
// the callback's list wrapper (D4870). The second value maps a list of lists through a nested
// `.map` that changes the leaf, so a result left at the source's rep cannot print the answer.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@VALUE@@
[1, 2].map((n) => [n, n * 10])
// @@TYPE@@
i32[][]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[1][1] + v[0][0] + v.length)
// @@WANT@@
23
// @@VALUE2@@
[[1, 2], [3]].map((r) => r.map((x) => x as f64))
// @@TYPE2@@
f64[][]
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v[0][1] / 4.0 + v[1][0])
// @@WANT2@@
3.5
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a list, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
